\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Overview.} One problem induces a \emph  {family} of decidable verifiers---a nested strictness ladder ($\ensuremath  {\mathcal  {A}_{\mathrm  {match}}}\!\supseteq \!\ensuremath  {\mathcal  {A}_{\mathrm  {uMFE}}}\!\supseteq \!\ensuremath  {\mathcal  {A}_{\mathrm  {pfe}}}$) on the MFE oracle, plus a separate \emph  {branch} for the pseudoknot oracle (pKiss). Which branch is \emph  {objective-aware} depends on the target: for a pseudoknot-\emph  {free} target the MFE ladder is objective-aware and the pKiss branch is unnecessary; for a pseudoknot target the MFE ladder is \emph  {out-of-domain} (it cannot represent crossing pairs) and the pKiss branch is the objective-aware one. ``Solved'' is thus whichever node one selects. Determinism does not prevent over-acceptance on two orthogonal axes---a wrong (out-of-domain) oracle (Axis~1, $99.6\%/28\%$ false accepts) and a too-weak rung (Axis~2, $92\%$ collapse). The paper turns this family into a \emph  {priced} testbed with a measured cost--robustness frontier and a sound cheapest-first routing cascade.}}{4}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:framework}{{1}{4}{\textbf {Overview.} One problem induces a \emph {family} of decidable verifiers---a nested strictness ladder ($\match \!\supseteq \!\umfe \!\supseteq \!\pfe $) on the MFE oracle, plus a separate \emph {branch} for the pseudoknot oracle (pKiss). Which branch is \emph {objective-aware} depends on the target: for a pseudoknot-\emph {free} target the MFE ladder is objective-aware and the pKiss branch is unnecessary; for a pseudoknot target the MFE ladder is \emph {out-of-domain} (it cannot represent crossing pairs) and the pKiss branch is the objective-aware one. ``Solved'' is thus whichever node one selects. Determinism does not prevent over-acceptance on two orthogonal axes---a wrong (out-of-domain) oracle (Axis~1, $99.6\%/28\%$ false accepts) and a too-weak rung (Axis~2, $92\%$ collapse). The paper turns this family into a \emph {priced} testbed with a measured cost--robustness frontier and a sound cheapest-first routing cascade}{figure.caption.5}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Claim--evidence map. Every headline claim is a \emph  {computed} measurement or a proof under a declared computational model, so there is zero \emph  {conditional verdict} variance under a fixed software configuration (candidate generation---and any commercial-API completions---remain stochastic); ``domain-dependent'' flags an effect this paper attributes to one domain rather than generalizes. The Axis-2 over-acceptance and cost claims are mirrored in SAT (properties of cheap-proxy verification, not of RNA); Axis-1's wrong-oracle failure is RNA-specific; the Goodhart effect is carried by RNA.}}{5}{table.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
