\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The verifier as a \emph  {graph}, not a scalar. Within one oracle, strictness forms a nested ladder ($\ensuremath  {\mathcal  {A}_{\mathrm  {match}}}{}\supseteq \ensuremath  {\mathcal  {A}_{\mathrm  {uMFE}}}{}\supseteq \ensuremath  {\mathcal  {A}_{\mathrm  {pfe}}}{}$); an out-of-domain structure class (pseudoknots) is a separate \emph  {branch} with its own oracle (pKiss), \emph  {not} a superset of the first. Treating a wrong-oracle target as a rung---rather than abstaining---is precisely what produces the $99.6\%$ false-accept rate of \S  \ref {sec:gap}.}}{6}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ladder}{{2}{6}{The verifier as a \emph {graph}, not a scalar. Within one oracle, strictness forms a nested ladder ($\match {}\supseteq \umfe {}\supseteq \pfe {}$); an out-of-domain structure class (pseudoknots) is a separate \emph {branch} with its own oracle (pKiss), \emph {not} a superset of the first. Treating a wrong-oracle target as a rung---rather than abstaining---is precisely what produces the $99.6\%$ false-accept rate of \S \ref {sec:gap}}{figure.caption.6}{}}
