\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Native positive control. Exact recovery of the annotated target from the \emph  {wild-type} sequence is low and predictor-dependent (a strict-criterion ceiling), yet native \emph  {crossing-pair recall} is high ($0.62$--$0.85$): natives form the crossing stems. Skeleton designs recover $0.00$ of the crossing pairs, so their over-acceptance is a genuine absence of the crossing stem, not a criterion artifact. Native and skeleton-design columns are single sequences; the DesiRNA column is best-of-$\le 25$ candidates.}}{12}{table.caption.21}\protected@file@percent }
