\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Axis-1 oracle validity. (a)~The false-accept rate on the same $250$ MFE-``solved'' designs spans $[15,60]\%$ across three pseudoknot predictors (dashed: the $3$-way-unanimous subset, $18\%$)---the \emph  {phenomenon} (large over-acceptance) is robust across all three, while the precise \emph  {rate} is a joint fact of designs and reference. (b)~Under pKiss the false accepts are dominated by near-misses: $35/70$ are within $2$\,bp of the full target (blue; the crossing stem largely forms), only $14$ are $\ge 5$\,bp off (red).}}{14}{figure.caption.24}\protected@file@percent }
