\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Matched-\emph  {wall-time} Goodhart control ($18$ targets $\times \,5$ seeds, robust $=\ensuremath  {P(T)}\ge 0.9$). Both arms get equal compute per wall budget; the strong arm runs $\sim \!\tfrac  13$ the steps (its reward is costlier per step) yet climbs robustness $12.2\!\to \!31.1\%$, while the cheap arm's robustness stays flat despite its proxy rising $44\!\to \!72\%$. Matched-wall-time DiD $+18.9$ pts---the between-arm interaction survives equal compute.}}{17}{table.caption.32}\protected@file@percent }
